############################################################
# v6 compute-unit weight calibration (per config, per budget level)
# Measures what an advance, a copy and an eval cost FOR EACH CONFIGURATION
# AT EACH BUDGET LEVEL, relative to one reference operation, and writes them
# where the rest of the pipeline picks them up.
############################################################
# SINGLE-THREADED and requires an idle machine: this is a timing measurement.
# currently in force: advance=1.0000 copy=0.1600 eval=0.0770  (no per-config profiles)
# suite=ab  underLoad=0  levels=[40000, 80000, 400000]  configs=18  cells=54
# reps=3  turns(=positions)/rep per level=[8, 4, 2]  warmup=6
# A repetition repeats the SAME positions with the SAME seeds, so variation across reps measures the machine, not the portfolio.
# Estimator: the FASTEST repetition (interference can only slow one down).
# Gate: the two fastest agree within 10%. Full CV is printed beside it as the disturbance diagnostic.
# reference cell = EMCTS@40000  (its advance is 1.000 units by definition)
